FRAMEWORK AUTHORSHIP

"Supportability Engineering" is an original methodology developed by
John A. Bowman. This includes:

  - The Supportability Engineering framework name and identity
  - The six-phase deliverable system and its structure:
      Phase 1 — Supportability Requirements Document (SRD)
      Phase 2 — Supportability Architecture Review (SAR)
      Phase 3 — Supportability Implementation Checklist (SIC)
      Phase 4 — Supportability Test Plan (STP)
      Phase 5 — Support Readiness Review (SRR)
      Phase 6 — Supportability Feedback Loop (SFL)
  - The shift-left cost curve analysis and phase-by-phase cost-benefit model
  - The template packs for all four volumes (Vol. 1–4)
  - The Baseline Standards Kit (Docs 1–4)
  - The AI Context File set (SE_AI_Context_Core.md and phase defaults)
  - The four-volume white paper series:
      Vol. 1 — Why the Best Support Organizations Shift Left
      Vol. 2 — Shifting Left When the System Can Think
      Vol. 3 — When the Builder Can't Sign Off
      Vol. 4 — When the AI Running Your Support Needs Supporting
  - The AOSR (AI Operations Governance Review) phase introduced in Vol. 4
  - The template prefix system (A-, D-, O- prefix conventions)
  - The SFL Incident Supportability Scoring rubric (1–5 scale)
  - The Shift Left Effectiveness Metric framework

